  "worked_solution": "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-{y}^{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3})-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (\\frac{2x}{3})-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (2y) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=6,$ $x=2\\sqrt{3},$ and $y=\\sqrt{3},$ and solve $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\cdot (\\frac{2(2\\sqrt{3})}{3})-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (2(\\sqrt{3})) & =0 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =-8\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
